    pr_ref:  # 10c3
    description: "FOUND 2026-08-11 while landing INV-safig. Reproduced, not inferred.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED. The change edited a SHIPPED DATA FILE — 20 rows removed from\n`packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/io_primitives/go.yaml` — plus two\nnew test files. `smart-test` selected TWO test files, ran them, and exited 0 in\n4.4 seconds. Running the obvious consumer suite directly then found two real\nfailures that the selection had missed:\n\n  test_io_boundary.py::TestLoadCatalog::test_go_catalog_tls_smtp\n  test_io_boundary.py::TestAmbiguousNameFiltering::test_go_qualified_run_still_matches\n\nBoth broke because they assert against catalogue rows the edit removed. Neither\nis exotic: they live in the single most obvious consumer of the file that was\nchanged, and a human asked \"what reads go.yaml?\" would name that file first.\n\nTHE GAP. smart-test's change detection maps SOURCE files to dependent tests. A\nYAML catalogue under `io_primitives/` is data that production loads at runtime\nvia `load_catalog(language)`, so no import edge connects it to its consumers and\nthe mapping finds nothing. The manifest it wrote for CI for this change contained\nTHREE tests, which is what per-PR CI would have run — so the false green was not\nlocal-only, it would have reached the merge gate.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN AN ORDINARY MISS. The failure is SILENT and its\nsymptom is a green tick, which is this project's recorded worst shape (\"a skip\nreachable by a typo is a green tick over a hole\", WI-jolif). It is also\nspecifically dangerous for catalogue work, which is where a lot of current effort\nsits: every io_primitives edit, every taint catalogue edit, and every\ncfg_nodes/*.yaml edit has this property. The two tests that broke here were\nthemselves ENCODING A DEFECT (they asserted a module hint no Go program can\nemit), so the miss also delayed finding that.\n\nNOT MEASURED, and it decides the size: how many test files reference a data file\nthat smart-test cannot associate with them. The candidate populations are\n`io_primitives/*.yaml` (14), the taint catalogues, `cfg_nodes/*.yaml`, and the\n`docs/io-primitives-overlays/` examples, which now have tests of their own.\n\nCANDIDATE FIXES, none built, listed cheapest first:\n  (a) TREAT A CHANGED DATA FILE AS A FULL-SUITE TRIGGER. Crudest, safest, and\n      the honest default given the silent-failure shape — if a shipped YAML\n      under a package's `src/` changes, run everything. Costs wall-clock only\n      when catalogue files change, which is not the common diff.\n  (b) A DECLARED CONSUMER MAP: a small table naming, per data-file glob, the\n      test files that read it. Cheap to write and immediately stale — the same\n      \"second home for one fact\" hazard this project keeps meeting.\n  (c) DERIVE THE EDGE: grep tests for `load_catalog(`/`load_overlay_catalog(`\n      and associate them with the corresponding data directory. Narrower than\n      (a), no hand-maintained table, but only catches the call forms enumerated.\n(a) is the one I would ship first, precisely because it does not depend on\nguessing the consumer set correctly.\n\nRELATED, AND THE REASON THIS IS FILED RATHER THAN JUST FIXED IN PASSING: the\nhuman is separately weighing whether `check-package-coverage` (a whole-package\nisolation gate, ~13 min local) earns its cost, on the reasoning that per-PR CI\nre-runs the tests anyway. This finding is evidence on that question in BOTH\ndirections — per-PR CI runs the smart-test manifest, so for a data-file change it\nwould have run three tests and missed these two; but `check-package-coverage`\nwould not have caught them either, since it runs each package's own tests and\nthese failures are inside the package that changed. What WOULD have caught them\nis `smart-test --full`, which is what actually did. Do not let this item be read\nas an argument for the isolation gate; it is an argument about SELECTION."  # 10c3
    fields:  # 10c3
      statement: "A change to a shipped data file must select the tests that read it, or the selection must escalate to the full suite."  # 10c3
      root_cause: "Change detection maps SOURCE files to dependent tests via import edges. A catalogue under io_primitives/ is loaded at runtime by load_catalog(language), so no import edge exists and the mapping returns nothing. Reproduced: removing 20 rows from go.yaml selected 2 test files, exited 0 in 4.4s, and missed 2 real failures in test_io_boundary.py."  # 10c3
